  "source_commit": "7cbf7a0c32fca1badf05931879a37c3f8a2b03b4",
  "scope": "Full mathematical and literal-source-contract review of RFD1-RFD9. The stated classical Harish-Chandra foundations were directly checked in the primary Borel exposition; inherited FV, RQC and ARO statements retain their previous scopes. This supplies original RowsFinDim without a cuspidal, gap, rank or idempotence restriction.",
  "findings": [
    "RFD1: Borel sections6.5,8.4 and10 (printed8.5-8.6), pages17,23,27-28, give exactly the reductive-group admissibility, automorphic-form finiteness and L2-submodule consequences used. The fixed smooth compact-finite cyclic vector is auxiliary to the Hom bound. Closedness of the image of a nonzero bounded intertwiner follows from A*A=c. No full discrete decomposition is assumed.",
    "RFD2-RFD3: compactness and the finite normal core give one common bi-invariant compact-open level for arbitrary original locally constant e. The literal I coordinates inherit FV finite class-number and arithmeticity; quotient measures differ only by positive component factors. No strong approximation or single-component claim is used.",
    "RFD4-RFD6: finite completed Hilbert tensor construction preserves irreducibility, continuity and original four-vector formal degree. The coefficient convention is phi=d*conjugate(<w,sigma(g)w>) with inner product linear in the second variable. The convolution order x^-1*h^-1*y gives precisely m(x)*phi(y), hence self-adjoint idempotence and compression. The orbit-span Gram identity yields the actual bounded intertwiner for each projector vector, even for arbitrary nonsmooth w.",
    "RFD7-RFD8: finite Hom multiplicity bounds the original archimedean projector on K0-fixed vectors. Both finite-kernel invariances yield P0 Re=Re=Re P0; commuting finite/infinite weak integrals then put ran(Re T) in ran(T on K0-fixed vectors). This is the full source HH range, with all measures and supplied weak operators unchanged. No e*e=e or e*=e premise has been introduced.",
    "RFD9: specialization into ARO17-ARO30 removes only their RowsFinDim producer. Actual row ties, arithmetic counting, common-family conditions and other retained hypotheses are not inferred."
  ],
